			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1230669">
									

<p>I like this one but this: &quot;SCP-371's physiology and behavior appear similar to ordinary microscopic viruses, although with several adaptions that make it a notable marine predator:&quot; bugs me a little bit after all Viruses aren't capable of self locomotion. There is a whole debate about them being alive or not.</p>
<p>Now, a Virus that somehow is capable of self locomotion is ok for me as an SCP. It is the fact that because of that SCP-371 shouldn't have the same &quot;behavior&quot; of normal viruses, after all viruses dosen't have something that could be called &quot;behavior&quot;.</p>
<p>I saw this back on September when I first got here, I wanted to edit it. Didn't knew how, and decided no to mention it. Now I know to change that isn't a little change but a major one, so I bring that here.</p>
<p>Oh waoh, that got more long than I thought it would. Beforhand I apologize if there is any kind of grammatical or spelling mystake.</p>

